{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>משריש</b> — like <b>ותשרש שרשיה</b> (and it struck root with its roots); that it made roots." "<b>ואקב</b> — I cursed, like <b>מה אקב</b> (How I cursed). The meaning: I cursed his <b>נוה</b>, which is his house, that evil should come upon him suddenly."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The comparison is to Isaiah 27:6, though Ibn Ezra does not cite the verse explicitly.", 1 "The comparison <b>מה אקב</b> apparently refers to Job 3:1, though Ibn Ezra does not cite the verse explicitly."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:46.706619935Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}